#title()

= The speakers
*Nomai* was a family of languages spoken by the Nomai, a nation of highly curious spacefaring mammalian herbivores. Throughout their recorded history, the Nomai species organized themselves into clans, communities of families committed to living alongside and supporting each other. The Nomai's ancestors were a group of nomadic clans who rejected the social hierarchy and regimented lifestyle of their sedentary kin and left the Nomai homeworld to explore the universe. Each Nomai clan traveled on a Vessel, an advanced spacecraft capable of warping across interstellar distances. Every 10 years, all the clans would send envoys to the Nomai homeworld to share their findings with each other; these gatherings were known as Festivals.

Although speakers from different clans were often unable to understand one another, they could still communicate through a carefully-preserved logographic writing system. Additionally, a prestige variety was used to converse at Festivals. At the time Escall's clan arrived in the Outer Wilds system, their native variety formed the basis of the Festivals' _lingua franca_, and so the remainder of the documentation will refer to that variety as *Festival Nomai*.

= The language
Festival Nomai is a strongly head-initial#footnote[Preferring to place words _after_ the thing they depend on (e.g. adjectives after nouns, nouns after prepositions, arguments after verbs)], topic-prominent#footnote[Allowing a sentence's words to be reordered to emphasize the topic of conversation.] language with relatively flexible word order that defaults to V2#footnote[A word order in which the main verb appears after one of its arguments but before all the others.] in independent clauses. Verbs exhibit highly agglutinative#footnote[Agglutination is the process of forming words by directly joining multiple parts, each of which contributes a distinct meaning.] morphology, noun incorporation#footnote[The ability of a verb to form a compound word with its object (e.g. "babysit", "birdwatch").], and a robust system of nonfinite verb forms#footnote[For the purposes of Nomai, nonfinite verbs are verb forms that act as other parts of speech.]. Nouns are also versatile and can both modify other nouns and act as predicates. Festival Nomai has an unusual morphosyntactic alignment#footnote[Briefly, whether the subject of an intransitive verb is treated like the agent or object of a transitive verb. English is nominative-accusative -- it treats an intransitive verb subject like a transitive verb agent.] which bears resemblance to a split-S#footnote[A morphosyntactic alignment in which some intransitive verbs treat their subjects like transitive verb agents, but other intransitive verbs treat them like objects.] alignment but with two distinct types of transitive verb. The language also makes extensive use of nonconcatenative morphology#footnote[Changing a word's grammatical meaning without attaching affixes (e.g. "sing/sang/sung", "fly/flew/flown").] and both lexical and grammatical tone#footnote[Distinguishing different words or forms of a word by differences in pitch.].

#calepin.elements.callout(kind: "note", title: "Trivia")[
  The syntax of spoken Nomai was inspired by the branched spiral structure of in-game Nomai writing. In my headcanon, the branch points correspond to words or phrases in a sentence that become the topic of a new sentence.
]